<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2025-01-10.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="005208"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005208" label="[00:52:08]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">rkeene: have you tested your untar changes with M2-Planet?</span></div><div class="line" id="005604"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#005604" label="[00:56:04]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">No, only natively</span></div><div class="line" id="005636"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005636" label="[00:56:36]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I suspect it might fail</span></div><div class="line" id="005646"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#005646" label="[00:56:46]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Why is that ?</span></div><div class="line" id="005646"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005646" label="[00:56:46]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">since you defined variables inside blocks</span></div><div class="line" id="005653"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005653" label="[00:56:53]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and M2-Planet is not smart enough</span></div><div class="line" id="005657"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005657" label="[00:56:57]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">to deal with that</span></div><div class="line" id="005707"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#005707" label="[00:57:07]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Ah, I assumed that because the Makefile specified C99 that it would be okay</span></div><div class="line" id="005708"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005708" label="[00:57:08]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, I'm not 100% sure for if's</span></div><div class="line" id="005719"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005719" label="[00:57:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but definitely can't do it inside for loop</span></div><div class="line" id="005742"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005742" label="[00:57:42]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(M2-Planet would just keep trying to create a new variable on each invocation then)</span></div><div class="line" id="005756"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005756" label="[00:57:56]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, C99 is for GCC build</span></div><div class="line" id="005816"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005816" label="[00:58:16]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">anyway, try running it inside stage0-posix...</span></div><div class="line" id="005824"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005824" label="[00:58:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">mescc-tools-extra is a submodule of stage0-posix</span></div><div class="line" id="005923"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#005923" label="[00:59:23]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Well, creating a new variable is fine since, unlike within a loop where it should be created as part of the preamble</span></div><div class="line" id="010136"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010136" label="[01:01:36]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">rkeene: I'm also trying it now</span></div><div class="line" id="010144"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010144" label="[01:01:44]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">in fact we'll need to fix your M2libc PR too</span></div><div class="line" id="010208"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010208" label="[01:02:08]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> +&gt; ./x86/artifact/M2 --architecture x86 -f ./M2libc/sys/types.h -f ./M2libc/stddef.h -f ./M2libc/sys/utsname.h -f ./M2libc/x86/linux/unistd.c -f ./M2libc/x86/linux/fcntl.c -f ./M2libc/fcntl.c -f ./M2libc/x86/linux/sys/stat.c -f ./M2libc/stdlib.c -f ./M2libc/stdio.h -f ./M2libc/stdio.c -f ./M2libc/bootstrappable.c -f ./mescc-tools/hex2.h -f ./mescc-tools/hex2_linker.c -f ./mescc-tools/hex2_word.c -f ./mescc-tools/hex2.c --</span></div><div class="line" id="010209"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010209" label="[01:02:09]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">debug -o ./x86/artifact/hex2_linker-0.M1</span></div><div class="line" id="010211"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010211" label="[01:02:11]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Unknown type const</span></div><div class="line" id="010212"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010212" label="[01:02:12]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">./M2libc/x86/linux/unistd.c:139:</span></div><div class="line" id="010231"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010231" label="[01:02:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">remove those const statements from signature</span></div><div class="line" id="010305"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010305" label="[01:03:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and for untar build I've got this: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://paste.debian.net/1344658/">https://paste.debian.net/1344658/</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="010406"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010406" label="[01:04:06]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Hmm, 262 is `if(VERBOSE)`</span></div><div class="line" id="010519"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010519" label="[01:05:19]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">commit a8f46dfc9d8b63277028c17076ae73703c7206e7   Update to define variables at top of function scope</span></div><div class="line" id="010550"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010550" label="[01:05:50]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">we'll still need a new PR to M2libc though...</span></div><div class="line" id="010553"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010553" label="[01:05:53]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">can you create it?</span></div><div class="line" id="010620"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010620" label="[01:06:20]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">just change function to &quot;int symlink(char *path1, char *path2)&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="010636"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010636" label="[01:06:36]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Yeah, I was trying to get stage0-posix to work to validate it</span></div><div class="line" id="010805"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010805" label="[01:08:05]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Other functions within `stdint.h` use `const` FWIW, which is why I used it: int chroot(char const *path);</span></div><div class="line" id="010851"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010851" label="[01:08:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hmm, I wonder why it failed then...</span></div><div class="line" id="011051"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011051" label="[01:10:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">rkeene: but in the top level unistd.h symlink is the only one with consts...</span></div><div class="line" id="011145"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011145" label="[01:11:45]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oh ok, chroot and mount are not...</span></div><div class="line" id="011201"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#011201" label="[01:12:01]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/63">https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/63</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="011240"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011240" label="[01:12:40]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ok, thanks</span></div><div class="line" id="011248"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011248" label="[01:12:48]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I'm a bit puzzled when const works and when it doesn't...</span></div><div class="line" id="011327"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#011327" label="[01:13:27]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I guess that it doesn't work on declaration, but is ignored on definition... for some reason.</span></div><div class="line" id="011351"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011351" label="[01:13:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oh, that might be it</span></div><div class="line" id="011431"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011431" label="[01:14:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, let's wait for oriansj to merge this fixup...</span></div><div class="line" id="011450"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011450" label="[01:14:50]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">so rest is now working?</span></div><div class="line" id="011455"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011455" label="[01:14:55]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(in stage0-posix)</span></div><div class="line" id="011509"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#011509" label="[01:15:09]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I haven't got stage0-posix doing anything useful yet</span></div><div class="line" id="011612"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011612" label="[01:16:12]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">anyway, you need to update top level M2libc submodule there with your change (that's the one that is used in stage0-posix, not the ones inside other submodules)</span></div><div class="line" id="011624"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011624" label="[01:16:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and update mescc-tools-extra to your changes</span></div><div class="line" id="011631"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011631" label="[01:16:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and then run &quot;make test-x86&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="011641"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011641" label="[01:16:41]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(or some other arch, e.g. make test-amd64)</span></div><div class="line" id="012216"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012216" label="[01:22:16]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Hmm</span></div><div class="line" id="012246"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012246" label="[01:22:46]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">untar.c:195:ERROR in collect_local     Missing ;</span></div><div class="line" id="012324"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012324" label="[01:23:24]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">But <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/mescc-tools-extra/pull/25/files#diff-335bb9dace26b3eabf6f2278b2028c2e73083d18e6b0d1e5f916d6130d3ec8d0R195">https://github.com/oriansj/mescc-tools-extra/pull/25/files#diff-335bb9dace26b3eabf6f2278b2028c2e73083d18e6b0d1e5f916d6130d3ec8d0R195</a>    looks to be correct...</span></div><div class="line" id="012535"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012535" label="[01:25:35]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">FWIW, the C specification says that sizeof(char) is always exactly 1 -- any reason to use sizeof(char) ?</span></div><div class="line" id="012610"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012610" label="[01:26:10]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Okay, this is fixed by not using an array but switching to calloc() -- now I get a checksum error</span></div><div class="line" id="012743"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012743" label="[01:27:43]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Afterwards: rm -f foo; ln -s /dev/null foo; rm -f foo.tar; tar -cf foo.tar foo; rm -f foo; ./untar --file foo.tar; ls -l foo   =&gt; The extraction of foo.tar was successful  lrwxrwxrwx 1 rkeene rkeene 9 Jan  9 18:27 foo -&gt; /dev/null</span></div><div class="line" id="012857"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012857" label="[01:28:57]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas, commit 1bbd83341c904e40373a0cb6f0244146ac9c4c1b      Switch to allocating from heap rather than stack     confirmed to work with stage0-posix</span></div><div class="line" id="012920"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#012920" label="[01:29:20]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(well, modulo the changes in <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/63">https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/63</a>   -- which need to be incorporated to the submodule)</span></div><div class="line" id="013046"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013046" label="[01:30:46]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I guess to make it more readable...</span></div><div class="line" id="013223"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013223" label="[01:32:23]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">checksum error is fine, we need to update checksums</span></div><div class="line" id="013254"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013254" label="[01:32:54]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it's the last part of stage0-posix</span></div><div class="line" id="013258"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#013258" label="[01:32:58]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Left a comment here: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/mescc-tools-extra/pull/25#issuecomment-2581505741">https://github.com/oriansj/mescc-tools-extra/pull/25#issuecomment-2581505741</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="013310"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013310" label="[01:33:10]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">make Generate-x86-answers would update them</span></div><div class="line" id="013320"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013320" label="[01:33:20]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">though I'll have to update other arches too</span></div><div class="line" id="013515"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#013515" label="[01:35:15]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">All the binary hashes changed, I guess because of the addition of symlink</span></div><div class="line" id="020832"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#020832" label="[02:08:32]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, that's expected</span></div><div class="line" id="020835"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#020835" label="[02:08:35]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">M2libc changed</span></div><div class="line" id="024438"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#024438" label="[02:44:38]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and M2libc changes often impact *EVERY* program built.</span></div><div class="line" id="024554"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#024554" label="[02:45:54]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">M2libc changes merged</span></div><div class="line" id="025604"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#025604" label="[02:56:04]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and yeah sizeof(char) isn't 1 for all architectures</span></div><div class="line" id="034800"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#034800" label="[03:48:00]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">n</span></div><div class="line" id="034808"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#034808" label="[03:48:08]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">woups ssh escape fail</span></div><div class="line" id="042132"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#042132" label="[04:21:32]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj, If a C compiler produces something other than 1 for sizeof(char) it's broken</span></div><div class="line" id="043009"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#043009" label="[04:30:09]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj, Thanks for merging my PRs !</span></div><div class="line" id="193711"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193711" label="[19:37:11]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">rkeene: one more problem...</span></div><div class="line" id="193721"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193721" label="[19:37:21]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">./AArch64/artifact/hex2_linker-1.M1:154 :Received invalid other; SET_X1_TO_FCNTL_H_AT_FDCWD</span></div><div class="line" id="193733"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193733" label="[19:37:33]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">you didn't add aarch64 define...</span></div><div class="line" id="193743"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193743" label="[19:37:43]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">i.e. what is the hex value of it on aarch64</span></div><div class="line" id="193801"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193801" label="[19:38:01]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I'm not very familiar with arm64 machine encoding myself though...</span></div><div class="line" id="194030"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#194030" label="[19:40:30]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">other than that I think rest of the arches work</span></div><div class="line" id="213514"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#213514" label="[21:35:14]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas, Hmm... easy enough to add</span></div><div class="line" id="213527"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#213527" label="[21:35:27]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, shouldn't be too bad</span></div><div class="line" id="213540"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#213540" label="[21:35:40]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">FWIW, I just use an assembler to get the correct instructions</span></div><div class="line" id="213846"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#213846" label="[21:38:46]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">#define SET_X1_TO_FCNTL_H_AT_FDCWD 610c8092    -&gt;  which is     92800c61        mov     x1, #0xffffffffffffff9c         // #-100</span></div><div class="line" id="214231"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214231" label="[21:42:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, should be good enough for now</span></div><div class="line" id="214248"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#214248" label="[21:42:48]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/64">https://github.com/oriansj/M2libc/pull/64</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="214251"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214251" label="[21:42:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">aarch64 in principle would benefit from riscv style rewrite but nobody has volunteered</span></div><div class="line" id="214310"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214310" label="[21:43:10]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">you probably saw how in riscv64 we have individual opcode and register macros</span></div><div class="line" id="214317"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214317" label="[21:43:17]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">not the whole thing as in arm64...</span></div><div class="line" id="214424"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#214424" label="[21:44:24]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Yeah, it's certainly more convienent not to have to pass things back and forth between an assembler</span></div><div class="line" id="214518"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214518" label="[21:45:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it makes early riscv steps harder...</span></div><div class="line" id="214525"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214525" label="[21:45:25]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but later steps nicer...</span></div><div class="line" id="214534"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214534" label="[21:45:34]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, for riscv we didn't have much choice anyway</span></div><div class="line" id="214559"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#214559" label="[21:45:59]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">riscv machine encoding is quite complicated, with various bits of immediate constents scattered around..</span></div><div class="line" id="214704"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#214704" label="[21:47:04]">&lt;rkeene&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I don't have a RISC-V assembler or disassembler so I just had to guess at it... hopefully it works out</span></div><div class="line" id="230627"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230627" label="[23:06:27]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">risc-v works</span></div><div class="line" id="230815"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230815" label="[23:08:15]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but riscv doesn't need assembler there...</span></div><div class="line" id="230920"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230920" label="[23:09:20]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">with risc-v all the basic RV32I, RV64I and I guess RV64M opcodes are all already there</span></div><div class="line" id="230931"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230931" label="[23:09:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">basically written down directly from ISA documentation</span></div><div class="line" id="230951"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230951" label="[23:09:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(perhaps after conversion from binary to hex...)</span></div><div class="line" id="234202"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#234202" label="[23:42:02]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">rkeene: while you are at it with M2libc, could you perhaps remove UNTESTED comment from riscv symlink functions?</span></div><div class="line" id="234209"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#234209" label="[23:42:09]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I've just tested it on riscv64</span></div><br /></div></body></html>